course: dictionary
lesson: 2075
title: Words for voting and politics
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A constituency is an area of a country, like a district on a map. The people who live there vote for who will speak for them in parliament.
explain: «A UK prime minister is also an MP for one area, called a constituency; a US president does not represent any local area.» The words «called a constituency» tell you the name for that area. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? The answer is an area that elects a representative.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Put in "the area where people vote for their MP" in place of constituency, and the sentence still makes sense. That is a good sign your meaning is right. Check a dictionary when you are unsure.
fact: Constituency means an area of a country whose voters elect members to parliament.
fact: In the UK, each constituency elects one MP.
fact: Constituency can also mean the people who live and vote in that area, as in «my constituency».
fact: A constituency can also be a group of people who support someone or whose interests someone represents.
exercise: What does «constituency» mean in «a UK prime minister is an MP for one area, called a constituency»? | *An area of a country whose voters elect members to parliament | A group of children in a class | A type of school for politics | A national holiday
exercise: In the UK, how many MPs does each constituency elect? | Ten | *One | None | Two
exercise: Which phrase means the MP for a particular area? | parliament building | national park | *constituency MP | prime minister
test: «A US president does not represent any local area.» What does this tell us? | A US president lives in every constituency | A US president is an MP for one constituency | A US president is elected by one town only | *A US president does not speak for a local area like a UK MP does
test: Ella reads «my constituency» in a news report. What does constituency mean here? | A shop where people vote | A school for MPs | A type of election day | *The area where the speaker lives and votes
exam: In «A UK prime minister is also an MP for one area, called a constituency», which word names that area? | MP | prime minister | president | *constituency
